From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FoAKTEE <hw609@cantab.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:30:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(m6-plasma): add the AthenaK RAPTOR model with the
 BlackLightPlus plasma decode

- change: model/athenak/athenak_plasma.[ch] port primitive_four_vectors (AthenaK b^0 = u_i B^i) and plasma_decode (n_e = rho/m_p, Theta_e = (m_p/m_e)(p/rho)/(1 + R), |B| = sqrt(b^2) B_unit, sigma > 1 cut only, no floors) with the BlackLightPlus operation order, including the fused multiply-add chains of g u and b.b
- change: model/athenak/model.c implements init_model/set_units/get_fluid_params on the compiled metric (CKS or SKS); tests/athenak_probe.c samples a points file for the R06 comparison
- change: setup.sh -c=athenak (definitions.h from model/blp_analytic when present, else bhac; RT_OUTER_CUTOFF 1100; -m=sks); run/makefile includes an optional model.mk for model sources
- result: u^mu, b^mu, b^2, n_e, B, Theta_e, sigma, beta^-1 and the emit/sigma-cut flags bit-identical to BlackLightPlus at 3e5 points on s455, s122, s093; |u.u + 1| <= 8.5e-14, |u.b|/|b| <= 7.3e-14 [SOLID]
- verify: bhac build unchanged: R01 synthetic image bitwise identical
- next: end-to-end get_fluid_params on the SKS metric once M1 is merged (R07)
